# Line endings. This repo is developed on Windows and Linux at once (the core is
# Windows-only; the UI is built on Pop!_OS), so leaving this to each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting is how mock-core.sh ends up with CRLF and dies on Linux
# with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
* text=auto

# Must stay LF wherever they land - a shell script with CRLF is not executable.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Must stay LF too: tools/verify.js extracts renderer source with regexes, and
# a CRLF checkout must not behave differently from the LF tree the suite was
# written on. The anchors are CRLF-tolerant as well; this rule keeps working
# trees identical across machines in the first place.
*.js    text eol=lf

# Must stay CRLF - PowerShell and cmd are Windows-only here, and CRLF is what
# every tool on that side expects.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# Never touch these: line-ending translation corrupts binaries.
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.exe   binary
*.cer   binary
